/*******************************************************
 * GENERATE PAYSLIPS (v10)
 *
 * Runs in the Locked Payroll spreadsheet, after "Generate Bank
 * Transfer File". Copies PSG.TEMPLATE_FILE_ID (Employees,
 * Employees_Hindi tabs — each with one formatted sample block,
 * logo + signature as images) into a monthly Payslip file, then
 * clones + fills one block per eligible employee.
 *
 * Routing: WORKER -> Employees (NON-MIGRANT) or Employees_Hindi
 * (MIGRANT), via Employee Master. STAFF is handled entirely by a
 * separate function in this same file — see "STAFF PDF GENERATION"
 * section below.
 *
 * Eligible = PAY_ROLL "Bank Transfer Mark Down" has a real
 * timestamp (not blank/SKIPPED). Append-only per month via hidden
 * _GENERATED_LOG — re-runs only add new employees.
 *
 * Access: pmo@ runs directly, hrassist@ via Web App, others blocked.
 *
 * SETUP: set PSG.TEMPLATE_FILE_ID. Add menu item to the Locked
 * Payroll file's onOpen — see NOTE at the very end of this file.
 * The doPost action branch for 'generateStaffPayslipPdfs' is added
 * in PAYROLL_GEN_6, same place/pattern as the existing
 * 'generatePayslips' branch — kept consistent with how every other
 * action is already registered there.
 *
 * v4 CHANGES:
 * - Employees_Hindi now shares Employees' landscape writer/config
 *   (template layouts are now identical) — WORKER_LEGACY and its
 *   writer are gone.
 * - Staff block was 56 rows (32 content + 24 "***" filler rows
 *   baked into the template) so each employee prints on one page.
 * - PDF export removed entirely (function, config, and doPost
 *   branch in PAYROLL_GEN_6 all deleted).
 *
 * v5 CHANGES:
 * - Template migrated to A5 landscape, 1 employee per page, 100%
 *   scale (was A4: Employees/Employees_Hindi landscape 2-per-page,
 *   Staffs portrait 1-per-page). Page fit is now handled entirely
 *   by column widths / row heights / font sizes baked into the
 *   template.
 * - Staffs: the 24 "***" filler rows are gone (no longer needed to
 *   hold a full A4 portrait page). Block is genuinely 32 rows now.
 *   PSG.STAFF.BLOCK_ROWS / STRIDE updated 56 -> 32 to match.
 *
 * v6 CHANGES:
 * - Total Deductions (I20 on Employees/Employees_Hindi, I19 on
 *   Staffs) is now SUMMED from the 8 deduction values already
 *   printed on the payslip — same pattern already used for Actual
 *   Total Earnings — instead of being pulled from PAY_ROLL's own
 *   "Total Deductions" column.
 *
 * v7 CHANGES:
 * - Employees / Employees_Hindi: plain blank rows at the end of the
 *   block didn't reliably hold the A5 page break (same issue Staffs
 *   had before its "***" filler rows were added). PMO added two
 *   baked-in "***" filler rows at rows 24-25 in the template, so
 *   each Worker block is now rows 1-25 (was 1-22 + 1 blank spacer
 *   at row 23). PSG.WORKER_LANDSCAPE.BLOCK_ROWS / STRIDE updated
 *   22/23 -> 25/25 — BLOCK_ROWS now equals STRIDE, same pattern as
 *   Staffs (the filler rows ARE the gap, no separate padding
 *   needed). The writer's old "push one extra blank spacer row per
 *   employee" step is removed accordingly.
 *
 * v8 CHANGES:
 * - Staff are no longer processed by generatePayslipsServer_ at
 *   all. Category = STAFF employees are skipped in that function —
 *   not written to any tab, not added to _GENERATED_LOG.
 *
 * v9 CHANGES:
 * - Monthly subfolder: MONTHLY PAYSLIPS/<MonthLabel>/ is now
 *   created (or reused) via a new META_DATA key PAYSLIP_FOLDER_ID.
 *   generatePayslipsServer_ now creates the Payslip_<Month> file
 *   inside that subfolder instead of the MONTHLY PAYSLIPS root, and
 *   self-heals (moves the file in) if it already existed outside
 *   the subfolder from a run before this change.
 * - NEW: Staff PDF generation. A brand-new function,
 *   generateStaffPayslipPdfsServer_, produces ONE individual A4
 *   portrait PDF per eligible Staff member (100% scale, 0.25"
 *   margins all sides), saved into the same monthly subfolder.
 *   - Tracking is self-contained: a "Staff Email Master" tab
 *     (Employee Code / Name / Email / PDF File ID), seeded in
 *     the Template file so it copies into every monthly file
 *     automatically. The "PDF File ID" column (a HYPERLINK to the
 *     generated PDF) is the ONLY completion marker for Staff — no
 *     entry is made in _GENERATED_LOG for Staff, to avoid two
 *     tracking mechanisms for the same fact.
 *   - If a payroll-eligible Staff member has no row yet in Staff
 *     Email Master, one is auto-added (Employee Code + Name, Email
 *     left blank) so their PDF still generates on schedule; the
 *     blank Email is simply skipped later by the (separate,
 *     not-yet-built) email-sending step.
 *   - Processes ONE employee at a time: write block -> flush ->
 *     export that block's exact row range to PDF -> save to Drive
 *     -> mark that one row's "PDF File ID" -> next employee.
 *     A mid-run failure only leaves the unmarked ones pending for
 *     the next run — nothing to reconcile.
 *   - Reuses the EXISTING psgWriteStaffTab_ / psgBuildStaffBulkBlock_
 *     / psgBuildStaffHIColumn_ / psgReadLeaveBalances_ untouched,
 *     just called with a single-item array per iteration instead of
 *     a full batch. The Staffs tab keeps growing within the month
 *     exactly as it did in v7 (still stacked blocks) — it's scratch
 *     space only now, never itself the deliverable.
 * - No changes to Employees / Employees_Hindi routing, writers,
 *   row/column offsets, filler rows, or Total Deductions logic.
 *
 * v10 CHANGES (THIS REVISION):
 * - Speed only, no behavior change: psgLoadStaffEmailMaster_ now
 *   also returns nextRow (= lastRow + 1) and lastCol computed once,
 *   up front. psgAppendStaffEmailRow_ uses those in-memory values
 *   instead of calling sh.getLastRow() / sh.getLastColumn() again
 *   for every newly auto-added Staff employee inside the per-
 *   employee loop, and increments cols.nextRow locally after each
 *   append. Removes 2 Sheets API round-trips per new employee (e.g.
 *   ~80 fewer calls for a 40-new-employee month). Nothing else in
 *   this file changes.
 *******************************************************/

